2. Decaid's bundled profiles (test data)

   https://github.com/decentespresso/decaid
   src/steps/fixtures/bundled-profiles.json holds the 73 profiles that Decaid
   0.8.8 bundles, with their numbers as numbers. They are test data for the
   step editor and are not shipped in the skin's ZIP. Decaid is licensed
   under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later (Streamline's
   CONTRIBUTING.md names these as Decaid's terms).


3. D-Flow and A-Flow

   A-Flow, the profile family this skin's editor writes, was forked from
   D-Flow, the profile by Damian Brakel (Damian-AU on GitHub). The A-Flow
   generator and defaults in src/aflow/ are this repository's own code,
   written anew in TypeScript; the previous
   version of A-Flow, the Tcl plugin for Decent's old app, is at
   https://github.com/Jan3kJ/A_Flow. D-Flow has no licence file.


4. DSx2

   https://github.com/Damian-AU/DSx2
   Many ideas are inspired by DSx2, Damian Brakel's skin for Decent's old
   app. No DSx2 code or asset is in this skin.


5. Bundled runtime

   The skin's ZIP holds Svelte's runtime (MIT) and, for reading bean photos,
   Tesseract.js and tesseract.js-core (Apache-2.0) with their licence files
   and the English data of @tesseract.js-data/eng (MIT) in ocr/. The
   development tools in package.json do not ship.
